{"items": [{"owner": {"account_id": 2379120, "reputation": 606, "user_id": 2081586, "user_type": "registered", "accept_rate": 100, "profile_image": "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/9bc0242120dba0ee84491d590eded03d?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG", "display_name": "akoo1010", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/2081586/akoo1010"}, "is_accepted": true, "score": 3, "last_activity_date": 1401900419, "creation_date": 1401900419, "answer_id": 24043107, "question_id": 24035609, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "body": "<p>Please ensure that your API bundle is associated with at least 1 API Product.  </p>\n"}, {"owner": {"account_id": 3544666, "reputation": 31, "user_id": 2960933, "user_type": "registered", "profile_image": "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/206578b507ec43894e9a81505ee9e5b2?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2", "display_name": "Jacques", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/2960933/jacques"}, "is_accepted": false, "score": 3, "last_activity_date": 1401969589, "creation_date": 1401969589, "answer_id": 24059671, "question_id": 24035609, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "body": "<p>Have you used the trace facility to figure out which policy is failing?</p>\n\n<p>Most likely your API Key is not not associated with a product bundle.</p>\n\n<p>Go to the \"developer App\": Dashboard / Developer Apps / \nAnd check that the product you are trying to access is indeed listed in the products list</p>\n"}, {"owner": {"account_id": 8308025, "reputation": 134, "user_id": 6244301, "user_type": "registered", "accept_rate": 100, "profile_image": "https://i.sstatic.net/JI8yp.jpg?s=256", "display_name": "Amit Patel", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/6244301/amit-patel"}, "is_accepted": false, "score": 2, "last_activity_date": 1469517459, "creation_date": 1469517459, "answer_id": 38583419, "question_id": 24035609, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "body": "<p>Api key Approval at the time of creating product you selected manual select it automatically ,, your problem will be resolved</p>\n"}, {"owner": {"account_id": 135892, "reputation": 21, "user_id": 2121723, "user_type": "registered", "profile_image": "https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/c2c36fdecb6e53d721faace4ce322a31?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG", "display_name": "advait", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/2121723/advait"}, "is_accepted": false, "score": 1, "last_activity_date": 1428161281, "creation_date": 1428161281, "answer_id": 29448139, "question_id": 24035609, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "body": "<p>click on publish > products from menu bar, select product which is associated to your proxy. under \"paths\" make sure the path of your endpoint is listed if not click on edit pencil icon and add path and save</p>\n"}, {"owner": {"account_id": 6089221, "reputation": 1, "user_id": 4752131, "user_type": "registered", "profile_image": "https://lh4.googleusercontent.com/-VJsy2jVFyDY/AAAAAAAAAAI/AAAAAAAAAAA/Uz8AtwVCd4o/s256-rj/photo.jpg", "display_name": "api", "link": "https://stackoverflow.com/users/4752131/api"}, "is_accepted": false, "score": -3, "last_activity_date": 1428254171, "creation_date": 1428254171, "answer_id": 29459982, "question_id": 24035609, "content_license": "CC BY-SA 3.0", "body": "<p>If an oauth policy is added then trace session doesn't work... because you need to add a header which consists of access code which can be done in console. If you are new to Apigee then I would suggest you to go and watch the foundation training video especially Lesson 6 which explains about OAuth v.2.0 in detail.</p>\n"}], "has_more": false, "quota_max": 300, "quota_remaining": 288}